  "text": "2002B15 Give a brief account of\nthe mechanisms which regulate gastric secretion.\nList:\n·\nGastric secretions\n·\nPhases: cephalic, gastric, intestinal\n·\nTable of source, product and release\nstimulus\nGastric secretions:\nInto the lumen\n·\nWater\n·\nHCl and IF\n·\nPepsinogen and gastric lipase\n·\nHCO\n3\nand mucus\nInto blood\n·\nGastrin\n·\nHistamine\n·\nSomatostatin\nPhases:\nCephalic:\nPathway\nStimulus\nEffect\n-Enteric NS\n-PSNS\nCNX -> ↑local release of\nACh\nSight, smell, anticipation of food\n↑secretions\n-SNS\nT5-L1 via coeliac plexus\nAnxiety, pain, exercise\n-Hormones\nSee later\nGastric:\nPathway\nStimulus\nEffect\n-Enteric NS\nMeissner’s submucosal\nplexus\nLuminal macronutrient\n↑local ACh release\n-PSNS\nAs above\nRest, food\n↑local ACh release\n-SNS\nAs above\nAnxiety, pain, exercise, labour\n↓local ACh release\n-Hormones (see next)\nSee later\nIntestinal:\nPathway\nStimulus\nEffect\n-Enteric NS:\nEnterogastric reflex\nDuodenal macronutrients, H+, ↑osmo,\ndistension\n↓gastric secretions\n-PSNS\nAs above (+ superior mesenteric\nplexus)\n-SNS\nAs above (+ superior mesenteric\nplexus)\n-Hormones\nSee next\nSee later\nSecretions table\nCell\nProduct\nRelease stimulus\nEffect\nChief cell\nPepsinogen -> pepsin\nGastric lipase\n↓ gastric pH\n↓ intestinal pH\nACh (CNX)\nGastrin\nProteolysis (pepsin)\nLipolysis\nParietal cell\nHCl\nIF\nGastric peptides\nDuo peptides\nACh (CNX)\nGastrin\nHistamine\n1.Proteolysis\n2.Activate pepsin\n3.Kill microbes\n4.Reduce iron to Fe2+\n5.Stimulate pancreatic and biliary\nsecretions\nComplex B\n12\n(IF)\nG cell\nGastrin\nACh -> GRP\nGastric distension\nGastric peptides\nCaffeine, alcohol\n↑parietal cell activity\nD cell\nSomatostatin\nGastric acid\nDuodenal acid\nGIP, CGRP\n↓ chief cell activity\n↓ parietal cell activity\nE cell\nHistamine\nACh\nGastrin\n↑parietal cell activity\nMucous neck cell\nMucous\nHCO\n3\n-\nConstitutive (PGE\n2\n)\nIrritation\nPhysical barrier\nChemical buffer\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
